{
  "_source": "Redacted live capture from local devcontainer test HA instance, 2026-08-28. Trimmed from 17 devices/748 entities to a representative slice covering the real gotchas found during exploration: Deye's model is a literal glob string ('SG0*LP3'), Lambda's model is a firmware version, Octopus/OpenWeather have model=null. This test instance has no duplicate Deye device (unlike the production system referenced in docs/roadmap/v3.0-geraeteprofile.md). Includes today/total_load_consumption entities for the device-resolver golden test. Extended 2026-08-28 (I7) with a real Shelly Gen1 3EM (split into 4 registry devices – 1 parent + 3 phase sub-devices sharing one config_entry_id, no parent_device_id link at all) and a Shelly 1 Mini Gen3 (a plain switch, no power sensor at all – kept as the 'other Shellys are just switches' case, not used by any profile). Trimmed to the entities the shelly_gen1_3em profile and its tests actually touch, not the full ~26/~10 entity set.",
